WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.210
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here!

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:06.279
If you've ever had a pet, you've probably
wondered what it's thinking or what it gets

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:10.760
up to when you're not there, and that's essentially
the premise of The Secret Life of Pets.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.010
Basically it's Toy Story for our four-legged,
furry, or feathered friends!

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:19.589
There's lots of cool characters which are
interestingly designed and smartly voiced

00:00:19.589 --> 00:00:25.329
by a cast of well-known actors including Louis
CK and Modern Family's Eric Stonestreet who

00:00:25.329 --> 00:00:29.840
lend their vocal chords to the movie's two
main pooches, Max and Duke.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:36.080
I loved Lake Bell as fat cat Chloe and Jenny
Slate, who did the voice of Bellwether in

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:41.980
Zootopia, is wonderful as a super-fluffy but
badass Pomeranian called Gidget who adores

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.560
telenovelas.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:49.710
Kevin Hart is also just flat-out fantastic
as the incredibly fluffy and equally insane

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.140
bunny Snowball.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:55.460
And Albert Brooks, who you'll have heard as
Marlin in Finding Nemo and Finding Dory, is

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:59.410
reliably on form as the hungry hawk Tiberius.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:03.730
Screenwriters Ken Daurio and Cinco Paul, who
did Despicable Me movies, and Brian Lynch,

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.630
who did Minions, give us a script that keeps
the pace up throughout, moving forward with

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:13.060
plenty of action and lots of laughs including
visual comedy, animal behaviour-based gags,

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.520
and some amusing nods to other movies – speaking
of which, look out for my video on this movie's

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:18.880
easter eggs and references!

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.659
There are some superb set-pieces and montages
right from the start, where we're introduced

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:24.740
to the movie's main pets.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:29.000
There's also a clever scene which shows the
ingenious ways the pets get around the city,

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.929
to a crazy funny fantasy sequence.

00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:35.880
Directors Chris Renaud and Yarrow Cheney do
a good job keeping us entertained during the

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.369
movie's 90-minute run-time, though the film
doesn't quite have the depth, heart, or emotion

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:44.829
of Pixar's best movies, and its story beats
do feel pretty familiar.

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:49.579
Animation-wise, the movie's really bright
and colourful and gives us a rather beautiful

00:01:49.579 --> 00:01:50.579
version of New York.

00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:54.840
In fact, there's gorgeous shot that flies
through New York City at the start, giving

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:00.250
us all the typical sights: the Statue of Liberty,
Brooklyn Bridge, yellow cabs, the Empire State,

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:03.279
Central Park, and so on, but it's all gorgeously
lit.

00:02:03.279 --> 00:02:07.619
Basically, if you enjoyed the Despicable Me
and Minions movies, then odds on you'll enjoy

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:12.069
this too, Can definitely see them making more
of these movies.

00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:18.230
Oh, and right before The Secret Life of Pets,
we get a short film called Mower Minions featuring

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:23.439
everyone's favourite banana-loving mischief-makers
who prove to be as much fun as ever.

00:02:23.439 --> 00:02:26.220
It's nice to see them again ahead of next
summer's Despicable Me 3.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:31.760
So, to sum up: The Secret Life of Pets is
a colourfully animated, vibrant and energetically-paced

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:35.950
feature which pulls back the curtain on what
our pets get up to when left alone.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:39.700
In terms of story and emotion, it doesn't
quite reach the level of the thematically

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:44.650
similar Toy Story or the recent fellow animal
feature Zootopia, however, it is a charming

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:48.820
flick with some fab characters and voice cast
and a bundle of laughs.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.620
And we get an added Minions short, so what's
not to like?!

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.959
The Secret Life of Pets gets 3 and a half
out of 5 Flicks.

00:02:54.959 --> 00:02:58.480
Now, what did you think of The Secret Life
Of Pets and the Minions short?

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.310
And what would you like to see in Despicable
Me 3?

